From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:46:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Key sets per program

A helper (on MacBookPro13,2 a KWin script through mbp-touchbar) writes the
active window's class to /run/tiny-dfr/app. [[Apps]] rules in the config
match it (case-insensitive, a trailing * matches the start) and choose
Set = "fn" (F1-F12), "strip" (the expanded Control Strip) or the name of
an [AppSets] entry: those keys left of the collapsed Control Strip, the
strip expanding and collapsing over them as before. Each program starts
with its own state; without a rule or a class the layer file and
MediaLayerDefault decide as before. The sets are rows after the three
fixed ones, built like the collapsed row. A Set name that is unknown, or
an AppSets entry called fn or strip, is reported and ignored.

TINY_DFR_WHICH_SET=<class>,... prints what the installed config gives
those classes; the PNG preview shows a row per set.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
